<h2>How should the grouped settings be laid out?</h2>
<p class="subtitle">Same 12 fields in four groups: Profile, Preferences, Notifications, Security. One Save button submits everything either way.</p>

<div class="cards">
  <div class="card" data-choice="a" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">A: Stacked sections</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px;line-height:1.6">
          <div class="label">Profile</div>
          <div>Display name ____</div><div>Email ____</div><div>Avatar URL ____</div>
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Preferences</div>
          <div>Time zone ____</div><div>Language ____</div><div>Theme ____</div>
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Notifications</div>
          <div>[x] Email &nbsp; [ ] Push &nbsp; [x] Digest</div>
          <hr>
          <div class="label">Security</div>
          <div>[ ] Two-factor</div><div>Session timeout ____</div><div>API token ____</div>
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>Stacked sections</h3>
      <p>Headed fieldsets in one scrolling column. Everything is still visible at once; simplest change, no JS.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="b" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">B: Sidebar nav + sections</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="display:flex;font-size:12px;line-height:1.6">
          <div class="mock-sidebar" style="min-width:90px">
            <div><b>Profile</b></div><div>Preferences</div><div>Notifications</div><div>Security</div>
          </div>
          <div class="mock-content">
            <div class="label">Profile</div>
            <div>Display name ____</div><div>Email ____</div><div>Avatar URL ____</div>
            <div class="label" style="margin-top:8px">Preferences</div>
            <div>Time zone ____</div><div>...</div>
            <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>Sidebar jump links</h3>
      <p>Same sections, plus a sticky left nav of anchor links. Easier to jump around; wider page, still no JS.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card" data-choice="c" onclick="toggleSelect(this)">
    <div class="card-image">
      <div class="mockup">
        <div class="mockup-header">C: Tabs</div>
        <div class="mockup-body" style="font-size:12px;line-height:1.6">
          <div class="mock-nav"><b>Profile</b> | Preferences | Notifications | Security</div>
          <div style="padding:8px 0">
            <div>Display name ____</div><div>Email ____</div><div>Avatar URL ____</div>
          </div>
          <button class="mock-button">Save</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h3>Tabs</h3>
      <p>One group visible at a time. Least scrolling, but hides fields and needs tab-switching JS plus care that hidden fields still submit.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
